Subject: Fix: no star with "x3" in the corners when the HUD leaves (issue #68)
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A fix of the original game, always on and without a switch (owner decision,
2026-10-12). It lives in the tweak series so the faithful series stays retail.

The match HUD (hud_2.fen, the same file on all five discs) has a "Slide1"
slide, which brings the two team panels (captain icon, items and their counts)
onto the screen, and an "out" slide, which takes them off again: at a goal
outside a Mega Strike, when the Mega Strike meter or a Mega Strike starts, and
at the end of a match. The "out" slide does not move the panels of "Slide1"
but its own copies, separate library components with the same names, and
HUDOverlay fills in only the panels of "Slide1". The copies keep the
placeholders they were made with: a Mario icon and a star with an "x3" count
on both sides. The slide moves them from the panels' place beyond the screen
edge in 0.1 s, so for about 30 ms (a frame or two at 60 FPS) the star and its
"x3" flashed in both top corners as the real HUD vanished (issue #68: a
regular star never comes in threes). The original code does the same.

The two copies are now hidden, as HUDOverlay already hides the power bars and
score panels of the "out" slide. The panels leave at once; the clock still
fades out with the slide. Only the drawing changes.

diff --git a/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerHUD.cpp b/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerHUD.cpp
index cf93640..d1598da 100644
--- a/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerHUD.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerHUD.cpp
@@ -124,6 +124,16 @@ void HUDOverlay::SceneCreated()
         leftOut->SetActiveSlide("4:3", true, false);
         rightOut->SetActiveSlide("4:3", true, false);
     }
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port fix, always on (issue #68): the "out" slide, which takes the HUD off
+    // the screen at a goal, a Mega Strike or the end of a match, moves its own
+    // copies of the two team panels, and the game fills in only the panels of
+    // the "Slide1" slide. The copies kept their placeholders (a Mario icon and
+    // a star with "x3") and flashed in the corners for a frame as they slid
+    // off. They are hidden: the panels leave at once, the clock still fades.
+    leftOut->m_bVisible = false;
+    rightOut->m_bVisible = false;
+#endif
     mClock.Init(presentation);
     mScoreDisplay.Init(presentation);
     mCaptainMeter.Init(presentation);
